1
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:34,547
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece

2
00:02:34,547 --> 00:02:37,467
must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

3
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:41,787
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

4
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:44,907
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber

5
00:02:44,907 --> 00:02:46,507
after eating the gum gum fruit,

6
00:02:46,507 --> 00:02:50,147
sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

7
00:02:50,147 --> 00:02:53,547
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

8
00:02:56,587 --> 00:02:58,507
During their journey to the New World,

9
00:02:58,507 --> 00:03:01,107
Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island,

10
00:03:01,107 --> 00:03:04,387
which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

11
00:03:04,387 --> 00:03:07,947
There, they found themselves facing the new Fishman Pirates,

12
00:03:07,947 --> 00:03:10,587
who were looking to destroy the Ryugu Kingdom

13
00:03:10,587 --> 00:03:13,267
and instigated an all-out war.

14
00:03:13,267 --> 00:03:15,467
At the last moment, the Sea Kings arrived

15
00:03:15,467 --> 00:03:18,867
to stop the Noah from crashing into Fishman Island.

16
00:03:20,627 --> 00:03:23,027
Someone help! I don't know what to do!

17
00:03:23,027 --> 00:03:25,227
You won't stop bleeding!

18
00:03:25,227 --> 00:03:27,027
I'm afraid he's going to die!

19
00:03:28,507 --> 00:03:30,907
You can give him some of my blood!

20
00:03:32,507 --> 00:03:34,347
It's Type F!

21
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:35,907
Take as much as you need!

22
00:03:37,387 --> 00:03:38,787
Hey, Team Bay!

23
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:49,827
I would like you...

24
00:03:50,987 --> 00:03:52,427
to join my crew.

25
00:03:52,427 --> 00:03:59,627
The Secret Revealed. The Truth About the Ancient Weapon.

26
00:04:03,467 --> 00:04:05,707
The royal family has reached a decision!

27
00:04:08,507 --> 00:04:10,707
Free! Finally free!

28
00:04:10,707 --> 00:04:13,707
Screw you, Horty! Now who's in chains?

29
00:04:13,707 --> 00:04:17,907
I'm sorry that I was going to be a slave for the rest of my life!

30
00:04:17,907 --> 00:04:19,107
Thank you, straw-heads!

31
00:04:19,107 --> 00:04:21,107
I swear I'll repay you someday,

32
00:04:21,107 --> 00:04:23,987
after I become King of the Pirates!

33
00:04:23,987 --> 00:04:25,827
What? That's a bit ambitious.

34
00:04:25,827 --> 00:04:27,427
Hey, what's wrong with having dreams?

35
00:04:27,427 --> 00:04:30,667
Come on, players! I can set sail for the New World!

36
00:04:30,667 --> 00:04:38,067
Your Majesty! Are you sure it's wise to release Horty's human slaves?

37
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:40,067
Not to question your judgment!

38
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:42,147
But the hatred they have for Horty?

39
00:04:42,147 --> 00:04:43,947
They might turn against all Fishmen!

40
00:04:43,947 --> 00:04:47,187
We can't let such fears turn us into something we're not.

41
00:04:47,187 --> 00:04:51,347
This island has always been a welcoming, safe place for pirates to rest.

42
00:04:51,347 --> 00:04:54,427
And these humans never meant us any deliberate harm.

43
00:04:54,427 --> 00:04:56,787
We have no right to imprison them.

44
00:04:56,787 --> 00:04:59,987
Now then, as for the rest of the new Fishmen pirates,

45
00:04:59,987 --> 00:05:01,627
that's a different story!

46
00:05:01,627 --> 00:05:03,707
Ah! Don't cut my head off!

47
00:05:03,707 --> 00:05:05,427
Please spare our lives!

48
00:05:05,427 --> 00:05:06,907
Your Highness! Really!

49
00:05:06,907 --> 00:05:09,307
We didn't know anything about Horty killing the Queen!

50
00:05:09,307 --> 00:05:10,547
They lied to us!

51
00:05:10,547 --> 00:05:12,707
We got duped by a bunch of lunatics!

52
00:05:12,707 --> 00:05:13,547
That's the truth!

53
00:05:13,547 --> 00:05:14,907
It's Horty's fault!

54
00:05:14,907 --> 00:05:17,187
We're not responsible!

55
00:05:17,187 --> 00:05:18,227
Mmm.

56
00:05:18,227 --> 00:05:19,227
Oh!

57
00:05:20,587 --> 00:05:21,587
Mmm.

58
00:05:27,187 --> 00:05:29,027
From here on,

59
00:05:29,027 --> 00:05:32,867
I officially order you all to live here on the main island.

60
00:05:32,867 --> 00:05:34,827
What?!

61
00:05:34,827 --> 00:05:35,827
Hang on!

62
00:05:35,827 --> 00:05:37,867
You're telling us to live law-abiding lives?

63
00:05:37,867 --> 00:05:40,947
It could be a lot worse, better than working for Horty.

64
00:05:40,947 --> 00:05:43,267
Come on! You can't be serious, King!

65
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:45,627
We don't want them living among us!

66
00:05:45,627 --> 00:05:48,907
We won't feel safe to let our kids walk down the street!

67
00:05:48,907 --> 00:05:50,267
We'll be right back!

68
00:05:50,267 --> 00:05:54,747
To clarify, you will serve your time, of course, and you will work under the supervision of

69
00:05:54,747 --> 00:05:55,947
my army.

70
00:05:55,947 --> 00:06:00,947
I will provide you all with gainful employment to use up all that energy of yours.

71
00:06:00,947 --> 00:06:07,187
And from this day forward, the Fishman District will be sealed off and all entry prohibited!

72
00:06:07,187 --> 00:06:14,827
The dark side of the Fishman had been exposed, along with the true killer of Queen Otohime.

73
00:06:14,827 --> 00:06:22,827
The conspirator, Horty Jones, attempted to seize control of Fishman Island, but he failed.

74
00:06:22,827 --> 00:06:28,467
All thanks to a band of human pirates who happened to be passing through at just the right time.

75
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:30,107
I'll be right back.

76
00:06:30,107 --> 00:06:33,107
Hey, have you seen Straw Hat Luffy around?

77
00:06:33,107 --> 00:06:36,107
Well, he, um, absconded.

78
00:06:36,107 --> 00:06:38,107
He fled?!

79
00:06:38,107 --> 00:06:52,247
Why did you leave the plaza without saying anything?

80
00:06:52,247 --> 00:06:53,747
Are you running away?

81
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:56,427
We're not too big on attention.

82
00:06:56,427 --> 00:06:59,747
You saw how many spectators we had watching us fight down there.

83
00:06:59,747 --> 00:07:04,227
If we stick around, they'd just treat us like heroes or some dumb crap.

84
00:07:04,227 --> 00:07:06,227
Just the thought of it makes me want to puke.

85
00:07:06,227 --> 00:07:07,227
But why?

86
00:07:07,227 --> 00:07:10,227
Isn't it a good thing to be the hero of a nation?

87
00:07:10,227 --> 00:07:11,227
Listen up.

88
00:07:11,227 --> 00:07:12,227
I'll spell it out for you.

89
00:07:12,227 --> 00:07:16,227
A man who shares his sake with other people, now that's a hero.

90
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,227
But I want it all for myself.

91
00:07:18,227 --> 00:07:20,227
Keep your damn sake!

92
00:07:20,227 --> 00:07:22,227
And stop putting dumb ideas in her head!

93
00:07:22,227 --> 00:07:24,227
Why won't you join us, D-Bay?

94
00:07:24,227 --> 00:07:26,227
I know you've got adventure in your blood!

95
00:07:26,227 --> 00:07:27,227
Come on!

96
00:07:27,227 --> 00:07:29,227
It'll be the most fun you've ever had, I swear!

97
00:07:29,227 --> 00:07:30,227
He's right!

98
00:07:30,227 --> 00:07:31,227
Crew up with us, boss!

99
00:07:31,227 --> 00:07:33,227
It'd be awesome to have a former warlord with us!

100
00:07:33,227 --> 00:07:34,227
And helpful!

101
00:07:34,227 --> 00:07:38,227
Luffy can take a little break!

102
00:07:38,227 --> 00:07:43,227
I told you, it's impossible for me to join you now.

103
00:07:43,227 --> 00:07:45,227
But I am still grateful.

104
00:07:45,227 --> 00:07:47,227
It is an honor that you asked.

105
00:07:47,227 --> 00:07:52,227
I am certain that it would be the adventure of my life to sail the sea with you all.

106
00:07:52,227 --> 00:07:56,227
But I am afraid I don't have the luxury to indulge in such pleasures.

107
00:07:56,227 --> 00:08:03,227
I have responsibilities that I must fulfill, and I've put them off long enough as it is.

108
00:08:03,227 --> 00:08:14,227
Once I've seen, to my duties, when I'm free from my sworn obligations, I promise I'll set sail and seek you out, no matter where you may be.

109
00:08:14,227 --> 00:08:25,227
And if you haven't changed your mind and still wish for me to become a member of your crew, well, I'll gladly take you up on your offer then, if you see fit to have me.

110
00:08:25,227 --> 00:08:27,227
You better keep that promise!

111
00:08:32,227 --> 00:08:33,227
Whoa, hey!

112
00:08:33,227 --> 00:08:35,227
A man's gotta do what a man's gotta do.

113
00:08:35,227 --> 00:08:37,227
